9277	{"artifactId":"LLD-57a2ba4d5f18c356-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-57a2ba4d5f18c356-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:40:20.341Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The request (always show the progress bar, with an idle look when no turn runs, working look unchanged, and no change to when a turn starts or ends) is fully designed, and the turn lifecycle (setRunning, Stop, done handling) is left alone.","evidence":"The design turns the hidden attribute, the [hidden] rule and hideProgress into an idle state at the three existing call sites (chat-panel.ts:1296, :1322, :1344). It leaves setRunning (chat-panel.ts:1256) and the done/error gating untouched, and it records the informational-done limit as known and not fixed here. There are no owner ACs. ac1-ac3 are derived and flagged as such in open question ts1. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the widget is rendered with `hidden`, hidden by `#insrc-progress[hidden]{display:none;}`; setProgress un-hides it and starts the elapsed timer once per turn, and hideProgress hides it, clears the timer and empties the elapsed text.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1381 `<div id=\"insrc-progress\" class=\"progress\" hidden>`; :1008 `#insrc-progress[hidden]{display:none;}`; :1268 `function setProgress(text){if(prog){prog.hidden=false;...if(!progTimer){progT0=Date.now();...}}}`; :1269 `function hideProgress(){if(prog)prog.hidden=true;if(progTimer){clearInterval(progTimer);progTimer=null;}if(progElapsed)progElapsed.textContent='';}`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"hideProgress is called on exactly three events (turn-event done/error, session-restored, and the Stop click), and setProgress is called on turn-running, on status events while running, and on submit.","evidence":"hideProgress: :1296 `if(ev&&(ev.kind==='done'||ev.kind==='error')){setRunning(false);hideProgress();}`, :1322 (session restore: `hs.value=cur;setRunning(false);hideProgress();`), :1344 (Stop: `setRunning(false);hideProgress();`). setProgress: :1291 (status, gated on running), :1307 (turn-running), :1339 (doSubmit when the queue is off). No other caller exists in vscode-plugin. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The widget is rendered unconditionally, so it shows even with no session or no provider.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1381 emits the #insrc-progress div with no condition. The outbox right after it is the conditional part (`deps.queue === undefined ? '' : ...`). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"setIdle is new (it is a rename of hideProgress), and the reused mechanism (setting className as setRunning does for the send button) exists.","evidence":"There is no setIdle anywhere in vscode-plugin. chat-panel.ts:1256 setRunning does `sendBtn.className=r?'stop':''`. Caveat for the build: #insrc-progress also carries class `progress`, so a className write must keep it ('progress idle' / 'progress'). The design leaves this to the builder and does not get it wrong. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The list of change sites is complete: chat-panel.ts (markup, CSS, script), chat-panel.test.ts (:1621, :1807-1825), chat-theme.test.ts plus chat-theme-before.json, and the chat-shell.test.ts harness.","evidence":"A grep for hideProgress|insrc-progress across vscode-plugin finds only chat-panel.ts, chat-panel.test.ts, chat-theme.test.ts and chat-theme-before.json. chat-panel.test.ts:1621 pins `setRunning(false);hideProgress();` in Stop. :1819 pins `<div id=\"insrc-progress\" class=\"progress\" hidden>`. :1825 pins done/error `hideProgress();`. chat-shell.test.ts:503 pins only setProgress('working…') and is unaffected, as the design says. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"chat-theme.test.ts fails on any removed selector and pins the exact list of added ones, so the removal of #insrc-progress[hidden] and the new idle selectors and keyframes need baseline updates.","evidence":"chat-theme.test.ts:333 `assert.deepEqual(before.selectors.filter((s) => !now.has(s)), [], 'no selector was removed or renamed')`. :334 deep-equals the exact sorted list of added selectors. chat-theme-before.json:15 lists `#insrc-progress[hidden]`. The selectors() helper (:68-78) records top-level at-rules such as `@keyframes ...` as selectors, so a new keyframes name must be listed, as the design states. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-theme.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-theme-before.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No stored data or message shape changes. The widget is live-only and never persisted.","evidence":"The widget is a static div in renderShell (chat-panel.ts:1381) driven only by script functions (:1268-1269). No store, message type or payload references it. The ids baseline (chat-theme-before.json:157 'insrc-progress') keeps the id unchanged. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A missing widget element is handled by the existing null guards, so setProgress and setIdle do nothing.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1260-1261 `const prog=document.getElementById('insrc-progress');const progLabel=prog?prog.querySelector('.plabel'):null;`. :1268 and :1269 guard with `if(prog)` and `if(progElapsed)`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reduced motion stops the working animation today, so an idle rule placed alongside it can be stopped the same way.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:1014 `@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){#insrc-progress .spin i{animation:none;opacity:.7;}}`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shell test harness cannot read the widget's class or label today (classList is inert and querySelector returns a fresh span), so it must be extended, as the design states.","evidence":"chat-shell.test.ts:70 `s['classList'] = { add() {}, remove() {}, toggle() {}, contains: () => false };`. :78 `e['querySelector'] = () => dress(bodyStub('span'));`. className is readable on stubs (:188 byClass uses n.className), which supports the design's className fallback. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-shell.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each derived criterion (ac1 never hidden through its states, ac2 idle animation and reduced motion, ac3 one widget above the input starting idle) maps to a named test in an existing suite.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping names a chat-shell.test.ts state-walk test (ac1), a chat-theme.test.ts idle-variant test (ac2) and a chat-panel.test.ts markup test (ac3). These replace the existing 'S002 ac3 ... hidden at rest' test at chat-panel.test.ts:1807. chat-theme.test.ts already has a has() helper used at :237 and :293 for the widget's colours. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-theme.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T19:40:20.341Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
